@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
    Layout = "_AuthLayout";
}

<div class="auth-head">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>What MyFinances keeps about you, and what it does with it.</p>
</div>

<div class="privacy-text">

    <h2>What is kept</h2>
    <p>
        Your name, email address and settings, and the records you enter:
        accounts, transactions, budgets, goals, debts, bills, assets and any
        receipts you upload. Nothing else is collected and there is no
        tracking or advertising.
    </p>

    <h2>Signing in with Google, GitHub, Facebook or X</h2>
    <p>
        If you sign in with one of these, MyFinances receives only your
        name, your email address (where the service shares it) and an
        identifier for your account there. It uses them to open your
        account and recognise you next time. It does not post anything,
        read your contacts or reach anything else in that account.
    </p>

    <h2>Who can see it</h2>
    <p>
        Only you. Each account sees its own records and nobody else's.
        Your data is never sold or shared. It is stored on the servers
        that run MyFinances (Render for the app, Neon for the database).
    </p>

    <h2>Your copy and deleting it</h2>
    <p>
        Under <em>Settings</em> you can download everything as a file.
        Under <em>My profile → Personal data</em> you can delete your account,
        which removes all your records at once. You can also unlink a
        sign-in service there, or remove MyFinances from that service's own
        settings.
    </p>

</div>

<p class="auth-switch">
    <a asp-area="Identity" asp-page="/Account/Login">Back to sign in</a>
</p>
